{
 "text": " Me and my kid are rebooting the Jaws series. Here's every plot from Jaws 5 to Jaws 10. We're gonna start with Jaws 5 and let's just pretend Jaws 3 and 4 never happened. We open on Amity Island. A steamship authority ferry gets rammed by a shark and starts sinking. People hit the water and a whole swarm of great white sharks start gobbling them up. It's friggin' Shark 911. Police Chief Brody, still alive and played by Pedro Pascal, rounds up every boat in the harbor like it's the friggin' evacuation at Dunkirk. Most of them get rammed and sunk. Only a few people make it back and the story's a heroine. It makes national news and brings in Chief oceanographer Jesse, played by Jesse Plemons, who wears a Steve Zissou red cap even though it's summertime. He brings an advanced radar that shows the sharks moving in a straight line. So Police Chief Brody builds a mechanical shark submarine, blends in, and follows the sharks to a giant underwater cave right underneath the Flying Horses carousel. They hatch a plan, lure all the sharks in with bait, which is thrown up by the mechanical shark submarine, blow up the cave entrance, then kick the kids off the carousel, drill straight down and pump all the water out. It's a crazy plan, but just crazy enough to work. Police Chief Brody and Jesse save the day. The radar goes quiet. Then, all of a sudden, beep, beep, beep, another line of sharks, headed straight for Edgertown Harbor. And that leads us to Jaws 6.",
